["I need to make 24 using 8, 5, 5, 9 with basic operations.\n\nLet me try combinations:\n- 8 * (9 - 5 - 5) = 8 * (-1) = -8. No.\n- 8 + 5 + 5 + 9 = 27. No.\n- 8 * 5 - 5 - 9 = 40 - 14 = 26. No.\n- 8 * 5 + 5 - 9 = 40 + 5 - 9 = 36. No.\n- 8 * 5 - 5 + 9 = 44. No.\n- 8 * 9 - 5 * 5 = 72 - 25 = 47. No.\n- 8 + 9 + 5 + 5 = 27. No.\n- 8 * 9 / 5 + 5 = 72/5 + 5 = 19.4. No.\n- 8 * 9 / 5 - 5 = 14.4 - 5 = 9.4. No.\n- 8 * (5 - 9/5) = 8 * (5 - 1.8) = 8 * 3.2 = 25.6. No.\n- 8 * (5 + 9/5) = 8 * 6.8 = 54.4. No.\n- 8 * (9 - 5) + 5 = 32 + 5 = 37. No.\n- 8 * (9 - 5) - 5 = 32 - 5 = 27. No.\n- 8 * (9 - 5) * 5 = 160. No.\n- 8 + 5 * 5 - 9 = 8 + 25 - 9 = 24. Yes!\n\nLet me verify: 8 + 5 * 5 - 9 = 8 + 25 - 9 = 24. ✓\n\nUsing each number exactly once: 8, 5, 5, 9. ✓"]